            <div xml:id="d937">

                <pb facs="0877" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg777"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860j.01/193: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wallace</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-28T12:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>280. Mission. Your 197, January 26, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="23" xml:id="d937-f1"/>
                    received this morning. Formal notification to Armenian Delegation of action of
                    Council granting <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> recognition was made
                    yesterday by M. Mil-lerand as reported in my 276, January 27, 7 p.m.<anchor
                        n="23" xml:id="d937-f2"/></p>
                <p>I have requested Foreign Office to inform Armenian Delegation immediately that
                    there has been a misunderstanding and that American participation in action
                    taken should be canceled.</p>
                <p>In view of what has occurred request Department’s specific approval of this
                    action and further instructions if any are deemed necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
